      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for pointing this out and it made me realize that this CL is actually undoing aosp/3125955.\n\nHowever, IIUC b/345658173#comment25, the issue seemed to have been with the \"traversal\" of the MMIO range. In this case, we don\u0027t modify the pointer to MMIO and `write_str()` traverses the input (regular memory) only while it bitbangs the UART register. So I don\u0027t think that bug applies here.\n\nHowever, from b/345658173#comment37:\n\n\u003e accessing MMIO with compiler generated instruction is likely to end in disaster\n\nwhich I suppose is the wisest/most pragmatic way to look at this.\n\nSo I\u0027ll instead add a wrapper around the asm.",
